# Security Validation Results
 
This document summarizes the validation activities performed against the Secure AWS Web Architecture.
 
The objective was to verify that security, availability, monitoring, and compliance controls operated as designed rather than relying solely on configuration review.
 
---
 
## Validation Summary
 
| Control | Validation Method | Result |
|---|---|---|
| Public application access | Accessed application through public ALB | PASS |
| AWS WAF normal traffic | Sent legitimate HTTP requests | PASS — Allowed |
| AWS WAF SQL injection protection | Sent controlled SQLi-shaped request | PASS — HTTP 403 |
| Multi-AZ application health | Verified both ALB targets | PASS — Both healthy |
| Application failover | Stopped one EC2 backend | PASS — Application remained available |
| EC2 public exposure | Reviewed instance networking | PASS — No public IPv4 |
| SSH exposure | Reviewed security groups | PASS — No inbound TCP/22 |
| Private administration | Connected through Session Manager | PASS |
| IMDSv2 | Reviewed instance metadata configuration | PASS — Required |
| EC2 workload identity | Reviewed attached IAM role | PASS |
| Secrets Manager access | Retrieved DB secret through EC2 role | PASS |
| Database network path | Tested TCP/3306 from private EC2 | PASS |
| Database authentication | Authenticated to MySQL | PASS |
| Database operation | Created, inserted, and queried validation data | PASS |
| RDS public accessibility | Reviewed RDS networking | PASS — Disabled |
| RDS encryption | Reviewed KMS configuration + AWS Config | PASS |
| CloudTrail logging | Generated/reviewed management events | PASS |
| CloudTrail S3 delivery | Verified CloudTrail and digest objects | PASS |
| CloudTrail encryption | Evaluated with AWS Config | PASS |
| CloudWatch health monitoring | Simulated backend failure | PASS |
| SNS notification | Verified alarm email delivery | PASS |
| GuardDuty | Generated and investigated AWS sample finding | PASS |
| S3 account public access | Evaluated and hardened control | PASS |
| AWS Config | Evaluated six managed rules | PASS — 6/6 compliant |
 
